--   fromCart y = (t, ρ, arccos(z/ρ), 2 arctan(y/(r_xy + x))) with ρ = rho y, r_xy = rxy y. The half-angle form 2 arctan(y/(r_xy + x)) equals the azimuth in (−π, π) off the closed half-plane y = 0, x ≤ 0; arccos(z/ρ) ∈ (0, π) when |z| < ρ. Mathlib’s arccos is clamped outside [−1, 1] and arctan is total; the theorems use the map only on domCartSlit where |z/ρ| < 1 and r_xy + x > 0.
