/-!
# Isotropic Schwarzschild, Cartesian form: the slit chart and its transported certificate (ATLAS-II)

Inverse map on the slit domain `domCartSlit M = {ρ > 0, ρ ≠ M/2, r_xy + x > 0}`:

  `fromCart (t, x, y, z) = (t, ρ, arccos (z/ρ), 2 arctan (y / (r_xy + x)))`,

(`2 arctan(y/(r_xy + x)) = φ` is the half-angle form of `atan2`, smooth off the closed half-plane
`y = 0, x ≤ 0`). `relation_sph_cart` is the first-release bundle `CoordRelation (gIso M) (gIsoCart M)
(domIsoChart M) (domCartSlit M) toCart fromCart jacCart`; `cert_cart_slit` transports the spherical
isotropic certificate to the Cartesian slit domain through the inverse relation
(`CoordRelation.inverse`) and the transport theorem. Coverage of the remaining Cartesian points
(the half-plane, hence the `z`-axis) is in `CartCover.lean`.
-/

